[{"id":"general-ability-4801","q":"4, 16, 52, 160, 484, 1456, ?","o":["3935","4","4381","4372"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Multiply by 3 and add 4 at each step: 4 × 3 + 4 = 16 and 16 × 3 + 4 = 52. The same rule gives 1456 × 3 + 4 = 4372."},{"id":"general-ability-4802","q":"16, 38, 21, 47, 26, 56, ?","o":["31","24","56","38"],"a":0,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Read alternate positions separately. The odd-position terms are 16, 21, 26, 31, increasing by 5; the even-position terms are 38, 47, 56, increasing by 9. The missing odd-position term is 31."},{"id":"general-ability-4803","q":"14, 28, 56, 112, 224, 448, ?","o":["788","806","968","896"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Each term doubles: 14, 28, 56, 112, 224, 448. Continuing gives 448 × 2 = 896."},{"id":"general-ability-4804","q":"3, 6, 12, 24, 30, 60, ?","o":["6","66","62","76"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Alternate multiplying by 2 and adding 6: 3 × 2 = 6, 6 + 6 = 12, 12 × 2 = 24, 24 + 6 = 30, 30 × 2 = 60. The next step is 60 + 6 = 66."},{"id":"general-ability-4805","q":"17, 20, 23, 30, 37, 40, ?","o":["51","41","43","30"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The differences repeat in pairs: +3, +3, +7, +7, +3, +3. After 37 + 3 = 40, add 3 again to obtain 43."},{"id":"general-ability-4806","q":"6, 5, 15, 24, ?, 71, 118","o":["43","46","47","24"],"a":0,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Each term after the first two is their sum plus 4: 6 + 5 + 4 = 15, 5 + 15 + 4 = 24, and 15 + 24 + 4 = 43. This also gives 24 + 43 + 4 = 71 and 43 + 71 + 4 = 118."},{"id":"general-ability-4807","q":"1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 63, ?","o":["120","127","125","121"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Multiply by 2 and add 1 each time: 1 → 3 → 7 → 15 → 31 → 63. The next term is 63 × 2 + 1 = 127."},{"id":"general-ability-4808","q":"6, 18, 42, 90, 186, 378, ?","o":["186","762","800","671"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The rule is multiply by 2, then add 6: 6 × 2 + 6 = 18 and 18 × 2 + 6 = 42. Continuing from 378 gives 378 × 2 + 6 = 762."},{"id":"general-ability-4809","q":"6, 9, 19, 32, 55, 91, ?","o":["135","150","154","142"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Add the preceding two terms and then add 4: 6 + 9 + 4 = 19, 9 + 19 + 4 = 32, and 19 + 32 + 4 = 55. The next term is 55 + 91 + 4 = 150."},{"id":"general-ability-4810","q":"6, 12, 21, ?, 51, 102, 111","o":["34","46","42","36"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The operations alternate ×2 and +9: 6 → 12 → 21 → 42 → 51 → 102 → 111. Therefore the missing term is 21 × 2 = 42."},{"id":"general-ability-4811","q":"5, 14, 28, 37, 74, 83, ?","o":["153","139","166","14"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Alternate adding 9 and multiplying by 2: 5 → 14 → 28 → 37 → 74 → 83. The next operation is ×2, so 83 × 2 = 166."},{"id":"general-ability-4812","q":"1344, 672, 336, 168, ?, 42, 21","o":["84","78","76","42"],"a":0,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Each term is half the preceding one: 1344 → 672 → 336 → 168 → 84 → 42 → 21. Thus 168 ÷ 2 = 84 fills the gap."},{"id":"general-ability-4813","q":"11, 20, 37, 46, 63, 72, ?","o":["89","11","75","20"],"a":0,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Add 9 and 17 alternately: 11 + 9 = 20, 20 + 17 = 37, and 37 + 9 = 46. After 63 + 9 = 72, the next term is 72 + 17 = 89."},{"id":"general-ability-4814","q":"7, 14, 8, 16, 10, 20, ?","o":["18","22","10","14"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Alternate multiplying by 2 and subtracting 6: 7 → 14 → 8 → 16 → 10 → 20. The next step is 20 − 6 = 14."},{"id":"general-ability-4815","q":"10, 17, 27, 40, 56, 75, ?","o":["87","97","99","40"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The differences are 7, 10, 13, 16 and 19; each difference increases by 3. The next difference is 22, giving 75 + 22 = 97."},{"id":"general-ability-4816","q":"3, 7, 10, 17, 21, 24, ?","o":["10","41","40","31"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The increments repeat +4, +3, +7: 3 → 7 → 10 → 17 → 21 → 24. Continue with +7 to get 31."},{"id":"general-ability-4817","q":"5, 14, 32, 68, 140, 284, ?","o":["503","572","601","571"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Multiply by 2 and add 4: 5 × 2 + 4 = 14, 14 × 2 + 4 = 32, and 32 × 2 + 4 = 68. Continuing the rule gives 284 × 2 + 4 = 572."},{"id":"general-ability-4818","q":"7, 14, 22, ?, 39, 47, 57","o":["29","36","32","30"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The differences repeat +7, +8, +10: 7 → 14 → 22 → 32 → 39 → 47 → 57. The gap is 22 + 10 = 32, which is followed by 32 + 7 = 39."},{"id":"general-ability-4819","q":"18, 21, 24, 36, 48, 51, ?","o":["53","24","55","54"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The differences follow the repeating pattern +3, +3, +12, +12: 18 → 21 → 24 → 36 → 48 → 51 → 54. The missing term is 54."},{"id":"general-ability-4820","q":"8, 11, 17, 29, 53, 101, ?","o":["197","178","216","195"],"a":0,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The differences double: 3, 6, 12, 24, 48. The next difference is 96, so the next term is 101 + 96 = 197."},{"id":"general-ability-4821","q":"2, 4, 7, 12, 19, 30, ?","o":["12","35","2","43"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Add consecutive prime numbers: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 and 13. These give 2 → 4 → 7 → 12 → 19 → 30 → 43, so the next term is 43."},{"id":"general-ability-4822","q":"7, 18, 40, 84, 172, 348, ?","o":["700","703","695","630"],"a":0,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Each term is twice the preceding term plus 4: 7 → 18 → 40 → 84 → 172 → 348. Therefore 348 × 2 + 4 = 700."},{"id":"general-ability-4823","q":"14, 27, 19, 31, 24, 35, ?","o":["27","28","19","29"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Separate odd and even positions. The odd-position terms are 14, 19, 24, 29, increasing by 5; the even-position terms are 27, 31, 35, increasing by 4. The missing odd-position term is 29."},{"id":"general-ability-4824","q":"2, 5, 11, ?, 47, 95, 191","o":["26","18","23","11"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The rule is ×2 + 1: 2 → 5 → 11 → 23 → 47 → 95 → 191. The gap is 11 × 2 + 1 = 23; the following term confirms it because 23 × 2 + 1 = 47."},{"id":"general-ability-4825","q":"3, 13, 43, 133, 403, 1213, ?","o":["3641","3643","3461","3652"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Multiply by 3 and add 4: 3 → 13 → 43 → 133 → 403 → 1213. Continuing gives 1213 × 3 + 4 = 3643."},{"id":"general-ability-4826","q":"19, 21, 23, 35, 47, 49, ?","o":["21","57","54","51"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"The differences repeat in pairs: +2, +2, +12, +12. After 47 + 2 = 49, add 2 again to obtain 51."},{"id":"general-ability-4827","q":"5, 11, ?, 47, 95, 191, 383","o":["15","14","23","17"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Each term is twice the preceding term plus 1. Between 11 and 47, this gives 11 × 2 + 1 = 23 and 23 × 2 + 1 = 47. The later terms 95, 191 and 383 follow the same rule."},{"id":"general-ability-4828","q":"2, 7, 13, 24, 41, 69, ?","o":["111","123","128","114"],"a":3,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Add the two preceding terms and then add 4: 2 + 7 + 4 = 13, 7 + 13 + 4 = 24, and 13 + 24 + 4 = 41. The next term is 41 + 69 + 4 = 114."},{"id":"general-ability-4829","q":"8, 17, ?, 42, 67, 109, 176","o":["26","25","27","67"],"a":1,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Each term after the first two is their sum. The gap is 8 + 17 = 25, followed by 17 + 25 = 42, 25 + 42 = 67, 42 + 67 = 109 and 67 + 109 = 176."},{"id":"general-ability-4830","q":"5, 10, 15, 25, 40, ?, 105","o":["58","72","65","71"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences","e":"Add the previous two terms: 5 + 10 = 15, 10 + 15 = 25 and 15 + 25 = 40. The missing term is 25 + 40 = 65, confirmed by 40 + 65 = 105."},{"id":"general-ability-4831","q":"27, 41, 55, 69, 83, 97, ?","o":["41","97","111","103"],"a":2,"s":"Number Series and Differences"},{"id":"general-ability-4832","q":"11, 13, 16